<div class="rt-prose rt-helper-copy">
<p>At times, you may find it best practice to password protect the pdf files on your account. This can add an extra layer of protection to files you do not want the general public to have access to. Password protecting your files can be easily accomplished using the option within your account. Here you add and remove password protection on your pdf files.</p>
<p class="rt-strong">How Does Password Protection Work?</p>
<p>It is important to understand how password protection on files work. When you choose to password protect a file, rules are created in your .htaccess and .htpasswd files. This rule specifies that the folder is protected and the visitor will need to provide the proper username and password to log in and view the specified file.</p>
{Msgs::Warning('IMPORTANT: When a user attempts to access the protected directory through a browser, the site will prompt them to enter a username and password. The name that you choose for the protected file will also display.')}
</div>
